{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"A complete guide to columnar data loading, O(1) indexing, zero-allocation row iteration, group-by aggregations, joins, and machine learning exports.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftDataFrame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an immutable, columnar data analysis engine built natively in Swift 6 for Apple Silicon. It combines Apache Arrow \/ Feather zero-copy memory buffers, O(1) schema lookups, and SIMD bitmask filtering.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["DataFrame (Value Type: Immutable Struct + Copy-On-Write)","┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐","│ Schema (FieldMap: O(1) dictionary lookup by column name)    │","├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤","│ Column 0: TypedColumn<Int64>   [ 101, 102, 103, 104 ]       │","│ Column 1: TypedColumn<String>  [ \"A\", \"B\", \"A\", nil ]       │","│ Column 2: TypedColumn<Double>  [ 12.5, 45.0, 33.2, 98.1 ]   │","└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"1. Loading Datasets (CSV, Feather & Parquet)","type":"heading","anchor":"1-Loading-Datasets-CSV-Feather--Parquet","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Load data from local files or memory buffers using streaming asynchronous APIs:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import SwiftDataFrame","","\/\/ 1. Load CSV with automatic delimiter and type inference","let csvURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"passengers.csv\")","let df = try await DataFrame(csv: csvURL)","","print(\"Loaded DataFrame: \\(df.shape.rows) rows x \\(df.shape.columns) columns\")","df.head(5).debugPrint()","","\/\/ 2. Load binary Feather \/ Apache Arrow IPC format (Zero-Copy)","let featherURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"dataset.feather\")","let featherDF = try await DataFrame(feather: featherURL)","","\/\/ 3. Load compressed Apache Parquet format","let parquetURL = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"telemetry.parquet\")","let parquetDF = try await DataFrame(parquet: parquetURL)"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"2. O(1) Column Access & Zero-Allocation Row Iteration","type":"heading","anchor":"2-O1-Column-Access--Zero-Allocation-Row-Iteration","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Access typed columns by name or iterate through rows using ","type":"text"},{"code":"DataFrameRowSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ 1. O(1) Typed Column Subscript","if let ageCol = df[column: \"Age\", as: Double.self] {","    let meanAge = ageCol.mean","    print(\"Mean Age: \\(meanAge ?? 0.0)\")","}","","\/\/ 2. Zero-Allocation Row Iteration (Bypasses heap dictionary creation)","for row in df.rows {","    if let city = row.string(\"City\"), let score = row.double(\"Score\") {","        if score > 90.0 {","            print(\"Top Performer in \\(city): Score = \\(score)\")","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"3. High-Performance Filtering & Feature Transformation","type":"heading","anchor":"3-High-Performance-Filtering--Feature-Transformation","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Filter datasets using SIMD bitmasks or transform columns functional-style:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ 1. Fast condition-based filtering","let filtered = try df.filter(column: \"Fare\", where: .greaterThan(50.0))","","\/\/ 2. Predicate filter closure","let adultFirstClass = df.filter { row in","    (row.int(\"Pclass\") == 1) && ((row.double(\"Age\") ?? 0) >= 18.0)","}","","\/\/ 3. Add calculated feature column","let engineeredDF = try df.addColumn(\"FarePerYear\", as: Double.self) { row in","    guard let fare = row.double(\"Fare\"), let age = row.double(\"Age\"), age > 0 else { return nil }","    return fare \/ age","}"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"4. GroupBy Aggregations & Joins","type":"heading","anchor":"4-GroupBy-Aggregations--Joins","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Group by categorical columns and aggregate numeric columns:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ 1. GroupBy with Mean Aggregation","let deptAverages = df.groupBy(\"Department\").mean()","deptAverages.debugPrint()","","\/\/ 2. High-Performance SIMD Hash Join","let employees = try DataFrame(columns: [","    TypedColumn<Int64>(name: \"id\", values: [1, 2, 3]),","    TypedColumn<String>(name: \"name\", values: [\"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\"])","])","let departments = try DataFrame(columns: [","    TypedColumn<Int64>(name: \"id\", values: [1, 2, 3]),","    TypedColumn<String>(name: \"dept\", values: [\"AI\", \"Cloud\", \"Security\"])","])","","let merged = try employees.join(departments, on: \"id\", how: .inner)","merged.debugPrint()"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"5. Exporting Flat 1D Matrices for ML","type":"heading","anchor":"5-Exporting-Flat-1D-Matrices-for-ML","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Export tabular data directly into contiguous flat buffers for machine learning training:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let (flatMatrix, rows, cols) = try df.toFlatFeatureMatrix([\"Age\", \"Fare\", \"Pclass\"])","print(\"Generated flat feature matrix: \\(rows) samples x \\(cols) features.\")"]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftdataframe\/gettingstarted"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataFrame\/documentation\/SwiftDataFrame\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"na